<title>USA: U.S. Treasury license rules on Iraq oil expected.</title>
<headline>U.S. Treasury license rules on Iraq oil expected.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury Department was expected to issue licensing regulations later Tuesday for U.S. oil companies' transactions in Iraqi oil, a department spokesman said.</p>
<p>The department's Office of Foreign Assets Control was in final stages of producing the regulations, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The department was widely expected to allow sales under a general license to keep U.S. oil companies competitive with overseas counterparts, as special licenses would take several days to process.</p>
